#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Score search ranking against labelled Loghub queries.

Indexes each selected Loghub 2k sample once (nesso), runs every query, and
reports recall@10, MRR, and nDCG@10. Relevance is a set of lines: the listed
LineIds, or every line whose EventId is listed.

Engines (--engine, repeatable; default nesso only):
  nesso     nesso search --json -k 10 for each --modes value
  grep      grep -n -F -i exact query, else OR of whitespace tokens via -e
  ripgrep   same rule with rg; skipped (not zeroed) if rg is missing
  bm25      stdlib sqlite3 FTS5, OR of quoted tokens, ORDER BY bm25(), rowid
  diy-faiss sentence-transformers MiniLM + FAISS IndexFlatIP (optional deps)
  xerj      Elasticsearch-compatible match on text (local xerj lexical node)
  xerj-neural  semantic query on semantic_text (opt-in; local model files)
  xerj-semantic  semantic query on semantic_text with xerj's default
            (lexical feature-hashing) embedder: xerj as shipped
  opensearch   single-node OpenSearch BM25 match on text (local node)
  opensearch-knn  OpenSearch k-NN (HNSW) over the diy-faiss MiniLM vectors
  ck        ck --sem over its own chunk index (skipped if ck is missing)
  vecgrep   vecgrep semantic search over its chunk index (skipped if missing)

Without --engine (or --engine nesso alone) the JSON stays schema_version 3 and
byte-compatible with prior nesso-only reports. Any other engine uses
schema_version 4 with an engines[] axis. Report-only: exit 0 for any scores;
non-zero only on errors.

Needle datasets (--dataset bgl-needle-100k, bgl-needle-1m,
thunderbird-needle-1m, all-needle) score each engine on Loghub 2.0 windows
whose relevance labels are the system administrators' alert tags, not ours.
They write a separate report kind ("kind": "needle").

Optional --measure (off by default) adds wall time, peak RSS (GNU time), index
size, and cold time-to-first-result. Quality-only JSON stays byte-identical.
With --measure the report is machine-dependent. Never a CI or nightly gate.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

